   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive tier IV membership in the New York state and local employees' retirement system to Michelle Merlino",
    "basePrintNo": "S4048",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4048-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4048\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\ngranting retroactive tier IV membership in the New York state\nand local employees'\nretirement system to Michelle Merlino\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill would grant Michelle retroactive tier IV membership in the\nNew York state and local employees' retirement system.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of this bill changes Ms. Merlino's effective membership date\nin the New York state and local employees' retirement system from\nMarch 18, 2010 to November 14, 2008 so she may be placed in the Tier IV\nretirement group. She shall file with the state comptroller a written\nrequest to this effect, upon the granting of such retroactive\nmembership, Michelle Merlino will not be granted a refund of any\nemployee contribution made by her to the system.\n\nSection 2 describes who is responsible for any past cost incurred in\nimplementing the provisions of this act.\n\nSection 3 states this bill shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nMichelle Merlino, commenced employment as a substitute aide for the\nDeer Park Union Free School District on November 14, 2008, which\nwould have entitled her to Tier IV membership in the New York state\nand local employees' retirement system. However, Ms. Merlino's\napplication to the New York state and local employees' retirement\nsystem was submitted inadvertently on a day she did not work. Once\nthe error was discovered she resubmitted her application on a later\ndate but was placed in the fifth tier instead of the fourth tier of\nthe New York state and local employees' retirement system. The late\nfiling was due to a clerical error on\nthe part of the Deer Park Union Free School District and not due to an\nerror on the part of Ms.\nMerlino's. She should not be penalized for the late filing.\n\nThis bill, if enacted into law would correct the mistake by allowing\nMichelle Merlino to file for retroactive membership in the New York\nstate and local employees' retirement system as of November 14, 2008,\nthe day of her actual employment.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nSee fiscal note.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nSee fiscal note.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
