    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4048A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\ngranting retroactive tier IV membership in the New York state\nand local employees'\nretirement system to Michelle Merlino\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis bill would grant Michelle Merlino retroactive tier IV membership\nin the New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill changes Ms. Merlino's effective membership date\nin the New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System from\nMarch 18, 2010 to November 14, 2008 so that she may be placed in the\nTier IV retirement group. She shall file with the State Comptroller a\nwritten request to this effect and, upon granting of such retroactive\nmembership, Ms. Merlino will not be granted a refund of any employee\ncontribution made by her to the system.\n\nSection 2 describes who is responsible for any past cost incurred in\nimplementing the provisions of this act.\n\nSection 3 provides the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nMichelle Merlino commenced employment in the Deer Park Union Free\nSchool District on November 14, 2008. which should have entitled her\nto Tier IV membership in the New York State and Local Employees'\nRetirement System. However, Ms. Merlino's application to the\nretirement system was submitted inadvertently on a day she did not\nwork. Once the error was discovered she resubmitted her application\non a later date, but was placed in Tier V instead of Tier IV. The\nlate filing was due to a clerical error on the part of the Deer Park\nUnion Free School District and not due to an error on the part of Ms.\nMerlino and, as such. she should not be penalized for the late filing.\n\nThis bill, if enacted into law, would correct the mistake by allowing\nMichelle Merlino to file for retroactive membership in the New York\nState and Local Employees' Retirement System as of November 14, 2008,\nthe day of her actual employment.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nSee fiscal note appended to bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
